NeoDEM TASK-223 -- the G1 wholebody sim had no floor.

Applies on top of 0001-neodem-g1-wholebody-sim.patch and the Isaac Lab 3.0 port already
present in the checkout working tree. Verified by three sim boots on 2026-08-28.

THE FINDING. The G1 was not failing to balance: it was free-falling. The wholebody scene
shipped a "# Ground plane" heading with nothing under it, so there was no collidable floor
under the robot's z=0.8 spawn. Measured, before this patch:

    step     0  z=+0.7865  proj_grav=(-0.000,+0.000,-1.000)   <- upright
    step    25  z=-0.7542  proj_grav=(-0.031,+0.044,-0.999)   <- still upright, below the floor
    step   550  z=-599.31
    step  4475  z=-39338.16

Delta-z grows by 0.0037 m/step, which is exactly g*dt^2 at the task's 50 Hz of simulated
time: textbook free fall, from step 0, for as long as the sim runs. projected_gravity stays
(0,0,-1) for the first ~100 steps -- the robot is perfectly upright the whole way down, and
only starts tumbling later as the flailing limbs impart angular momentum with nothing to
push against. Every "why can't it balance" hypothesis was being tested on a robot that had
nothing to balance on.

The warehouse USD does carry a collidable floor -- /Lab/Structure/floor, a 4-point quad at
world z=0 with physics:approximation="none", collisionEnabled=True, and an xy extent that
covers the spawn at (-3.9, -2.818). But it is spawned at /World/envs/env_.*/Room, INSIDE the
cloned env, while the task sets replicate_physics=True. Upstream's own (commented-out) ground
in the non-wholebody scene sits at /World/GroundPlane -- outside /World/envs -- which is the
placement that survives cloning. Hunk 4 puts it back there.

AFTER: z holds in [0.7825, 0.7919] -- a 9 mm band -- for the entire run, projected_gravity
(0,0,-1), no joint within 0.02 rad of a limit, leg velocities decaying to 0.24 rad/s. The G1
stands. The external isaac_gait_probe.py agrees over DDS: "base upright PASS",
"knees/ankles off their limits PASS", roll 0.007..0.019 rad.

It does NOT yet walk: a vx=0.5 command produces a small forward lean (pitch 0.08 vs 0.045
at rest) and no stepping. That is now a well-posed locomotion question rather than a
measurement artefact, and it belongs to TASK-203.

Four hunks:

  1. action_provider_wh_dds.py: obs_scales, env-selectable. This was TASK-223's lead 1 and it
     is REFUTED. Once there was a floor, both arms were run: upstream's all-1.0 stands rock
     solid, while Unitree's locomotion scales (ang_vel 0.25 / joint_vel 0.05) COLLAPSE the
     robot -- z falls to ~0.07, projected_gravity to (-1,0,0) (face down), ankles pinned
     28-50 % of the time, knees thrashing in antiphase at 3.6 Hz. The default is therefore
     upstream's all-1.0; NEODEM_OBS_SCALES=unitree reproduces the refuted arm.
  2. action_provider_wh_dds.py: _task223_log. Prints projected_gravity_b (a convention-free
     uprightness test no quaternion-order bug can reach), root height, true roll/pitch, the
     leg joints against their defaults, and -- once, at step 0, before the first action is
     applied -- the full articulation joint-name order. This is what found the free fall.
     Confirmed at step 0: old_action_indices == list(range(29)) and every action_to_indices
     entry is < 29, so the 29-vs-43 joint indexing is sound. That lead is closed too.
  3. g1_29dof_state.py: the IMU quaternion published to rt/lowstate. Upstream's
     assume_w_first=True was right on Isaac Lab 2.x and is wrong on 3.0, where the quaternion
     is (x,y,z,w). Combined with dds/g1_robot_dds.py:101 it made a perfectly upright base
     publish as |roll| = pi, so isaac_gait_probe.py's "base upright" check could never pass,
     on any hypothesis. Now validated end to end: with the robot standing, the probe reads
     roll 0.007..0.019 rad over DDS, matching the sim's own internal log.
  4. base_scene_pickplace_cylindercfg_wholebody.py: the missing ground plane. THE fix.

